<title>USA: Amoco makes another Nile Delta gas discovery.</title>
<headline>Amoco makes another Nile Delta gas discovery.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amoco Corp said Tuesday it made a fourth gas discovery on the Ras el Barr Offshore Concession in the Nile Delta.</p>
<p>It said the Osiris East-1 well, drilled 30 miles offshore in 287 feet of water, tested at a rate of 35 million cubic feet of gas per day and 2,275 barrels of condensate per day at a depth of 13,280 feet.</p>
<p>Amoco Egypt Ras el Barr B.V. operates the Ras el Barr Offshore concession, which is jointly and equally held by Amoco and IEOC Co Inc, a subsidiary of Agip SpA.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
